# Normalize line endings on commit, check out LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' `core.autocrlf=true` default rewrites LF to CRLF
# on checkout and corrupts the fixtures that assert on exact bytes: the CRLF/BOM
# tally in `packages/tools/src/lib/text.ts`, and every `apply_patch`, `diff` and
# `replace` test. Committing the rule fixes every clone, which a CI-only
# `git config` would not.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched by normalization.
*.png binary
*.wasm binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Lockfile: Bun's own format, kept verbatim.
bun.lock -text
